  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1116 AM MDT Mon Jun 22 2026\n\nUpper high centered over the Big Bend region and the Chihuahuan\nDesert of northern Mexico. On the southern margin, a couple of\neasterly waves move across central Mexico with no appreciable\nimpact on our area. To the north of the center are some higher\nclouds moving east across the northern CWA. Very warm 500mb temps\nof -1C to -3C, so capping of the airmass continues. \n\nThe upper high does become more circular by Tuesday and especially\nWednesday, allowing some sub-tropical moisture to move back into\nthe area. 500mb temps also cool, turning our airmass back to\nslightly unstable. Thus slight chances of thunderstorms return to\nthe area Wednesday, mostly over the mountains. The slight chance\nwill continue Thursday and Friday and POPs extend down into the\nlowlands. Hot weather will continue, with Tue/Wed being the\nhottest days. Heat Advisories out through Wednesday and may be\nneeded beyond. \n\nSaturday and Sunday...high center drifts south and west as Pacific\ntrough cuts through the central Rockies. This increases our west\nflow which scours out any moisture still left, and it induces\nbreezy afternoons each day. Unless the mountains get some\nsignificant rain, our airmass and fuels are going to go through a\nlong stretch of drying out. Thus with the afternoon winds, fire \nconditions will approach critical and possibly Red Flag conditions.\nStay tuned.",
